__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
!.env.dist
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
node_modules/
data/
# The docs now tell a reader to build a wheel and install it outside the checkout, so these
# appear the first time anyone follows them. build/ in particular holds a full copy of the
# package, which is how a stale second copy of the source ends up in a diff.
build/
dist/
*.whl

# Transient cross-process coordination locks created by runner._ledger_lock and the
# calibration session guard. One byte each, recreated on demand; never evidence.
*.lock
!uv.lock

# Playwright's own output. The browser suite is source; its report, traces and installed
# packages are not, and `node_modules/` above already covers tests/e2e/node_modules.
tests/e2e/test-results/
tests/e2e/playwright-report/
BUILD-REPORT.md
